"The postoperative pathology is reassuring, showing a Gleason 3+4 (ISUP grade group 2) with no extraprostatic extension and negative surgical margins. Furthermore, the seminal vesicles were not invaded, and lymphovascular invasion was absent. The biopsy identified Gleason 3+4 in the right peripheral zone (mid), with no high-risk features like cribriform pattern or perineural invasion noted. A significant factor influencing prognosis is the absence of documented nodal sampling, meaning the pNx status does not establish node-negative disease, which widens uncertainty regarding regional spread. Countervailing findings include the negative margins and lack of seminal vesicle invasion. The prognosis is heavily dependent on the postoperative PSA and its subsequent trajectory, which are currently unknown. Information regarding postoperative PSA and its trajectory would be crucial in revising this assessment. The fixed estimated horizon is 45.23 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 29.40–61.06 months; its coverage has not been validated."
